# Phase 18 continuation — Message property compatibility

- Started from clean branch `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate` at `e8fa4234`.
- Re-read the Phase 18 plan and Rust coding workflow. The objective remains full Java 5.5.1 compatibility, with API/setting parity and matching observable flows; plans remain unchanged.
- Reconfirmed pinned Java source `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`: `MessageAccessor.putProperty` and `clearProperty` delegate to a `HashMap` that accepts a null key; `MessageDecoder.messageProperties2String` serializes it as the literal key `null`. `MessageAccessor.cloneMessage` shares body and property references and does not copy `transactionId`.
- Planned next: add invoked Java fixture and Rust differential for a null property key, then implement storage/lookup/removal and cover every message-to-wire path. Keep clone semantics as a separate compatibility slice.
- Added invoked Java cases for null-key lookup, presence, clear, null value, and property-string encoding. A first direct exec used stale compiled classes and left the fixture hash unchanged; after `mvn -q -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml test-compile`, regeneration succeeded. Current message fixture SHA-256: `e774ee6cd0ef2b9538f648d93c87c75d0ddb84c14c081f1dc2279163a05ef9f2`.
- PASS: `mvn -q -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` completed; all pinned Java fixture drift checks passed, including 37 scenarios, the updated message fixture, and Java decoding of Rust-generated frames. `git diff --check` passed.
- Implemented nullable-key state without changing the existing string-to-string `MessageProperties` view. Added full nullable-entry replacement/iteration, nullable-key lookup/presence/set/clear, and Serde round-trip support. Stored-record and compact encoders, producer sync preparation, producer batch records, and Consumer retry-topic fallback now use Java's null-key-to-literal-`null` wire conversion and omit null values. Updated the Java fixture for `setProperties` with a null key. Current fixture SHA-256: `1c8eaa749d9b1d990e04520a5879c84b7d55dad99d8cf08c775afc4866a14f21`.
- PASS: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-common --all-features --locked` (21 unit, 17 message differential, 1 topic-validator, 14 doctests); `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer --all-features --locked` (142 unit plus admin, producer API, request/reply, scripted send, transaction integration suites and doctests); `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --all-features --locked` (219 unit plus all integration suites and doctests); after extracting retry-wire preparation, the focused `send_back_uses_live_facade_group_and_namespaced_retry_topic` test passed again.
- PASS: `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-common -p rocketmq-classic-producer -p rocketmq-classic-consumer -p rocketmq-classic --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`; `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; pinned offline Maven `verify` (37 scenarios and fixture drift/cross-decodes); `git diff --check`.
- Updated the Phase 8 method matrix, P8 fixture checksum, and release checklist. P18-V01 remains open for the remaining Java/Rust audit, including the separate `MessageAccessor.cloneMessage` shallow-alias behavior; full final-revision P18-V02, GitHub Ubuntu evidence, Phase 19 Docker/Broker automation, and release registry/version resolution also remain open.

- Selector snapshot compatibility slice (`a3993a8d`, 2026-10-15): inspected pinned Java 5.5.1 `MessageAccessor.cloneMessage` and `DefaultMQProducerImpl.invokeMessageQueueSelector` / `sendSelectImpl`. Java passes a distinct message with the configured namespace removed, copied flag/properties/body values, shared body/property references, and no transaction ID. Rust now builds that readable snapshot for both invoke-only and selector-send paths, retaining its owned deep-copy model because the callback receives `&Message`. Added `ProducerCoreFixtures.implementationSelectorMessageSnapshot`, updated the Producer/Message matrices and release checklist, and regenerated `fixtures/producer/core.json` (SHA-256 `41dd9cca0b559e68397eb2d7bd41769596417ac0d0be605b8cd586423524b1d1`). The scripted differential covers an already-namespaced input, callback-visible body/flag/property/topic/transaction ID, and input preservation.
- Validation: `mvn -q -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml -Dproducer.core.fixture.verify=false verify` PASS (37 scenarios and generated fixture); `mvn -q -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` PASS (37 scenarios, fixture drift checks and Java/Rust cross-decodes); `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer --all-features --locked` PASS (142 unit, 10 admin, 27 Producer API, 3 request/reply, 17 scripted-send, 7 transaction tests and 6 doctests); strict Producer all-target/all-feature Clippy PASS; `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` PASS. An initial direct `exec:java` fixture command invoked `compat.Main` and returned its usage text; no fixture was changed by that failed invocation.
- This closes the selector snapshot slice only. Broad P18-V01 source/API/input/error/flow and reverse-export reconciliation remains open; full final-revision P18-V02, current-revision GitHub Ubuntu address-profile evidence, Phase 19 local Docker/Broker automation, native Windows runtime evidence and pre-publication registry/version checks remain outstanding.

- MessageAccessor.deepCopyProperties compatibility slice (`2026-10-15`): added invoked Java 5.5.1 fixture coverage for null maps, null keys/values, distinct copied map state, and independent mutations; the Rust differential uses `NullableMessageProperties::clone` / `Option::clone` without adding a wrapper API. Updated the Phase 8 method matrix, message fixture checksum, and release checklist. Fixture SHA-256: `bb82ac0033f97b109251a178330b278f86257ed2ad34a8f198fe597002dd7902`.
- Validation: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-common --all-features --locked` PASS (21 unit, 17 message differential, 1 topic-validator, 14 doctests); `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-common --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` PASS; `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` PASS; pinned offline Maven `verify` PASS (37 scenarios, fixture drift, Java/Rust cross-decodes); checksum matches the matrix and manifest.

- MessageAccessor helper getter/setter audit slice (`2026-10-15`): source-scanned all public `MessageAccessor` methods in the pinned Java 5.5.1 source. The invoked `messagePublicApi` fixture now calls transfer/correction/origin-ID/MQ2/reconsume/max-reconsume/consume-start getter/setter pairs and checks the nullable transfer-flag entry. Rust compares each Java result through the mapped public property constants and property accessors. Updated the Phase 8 matrix, fixture checksum, and release checklist; this closes these value paths only, while broad P18-V01 remains open. Fixture SHA-256: `a4624b439f6debb59c83deb88927c4577daa75c2900564ae366b114f43baedd2`.
- Validation: pinned offline Maven `verify` PASS (37 scenarios, fixture drift, Java/Rust cross-decodes); `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-common --all-features --locked` PASS (21 unit, 17 message differential, 1 topic-validator, 14 doctests); strict Common all-target/all-feature Clippy PASS; format, diff and fixture checksum checks PASS. The first Rust differential compile caught comparing a `serde_json::Value` directly with `Option<&str>`; changed the assertion to compare its parsed string value and reran all Common checks successfully. The initial Maven `exec:java` regeneration attempt selected `compat.Main` and returned its usage text without writing the fixture; direct launch of `compat.MessageDecodeFixtures` with the Maven-built classpath generated the fixture successfully.

- MessageExt scalar public API audit slice (`2026-10-15`): the source-to-Rust inventory now has direct invoked Java 5.5.1 and Rust differential coverage for default values and setters/getters of queue ID, born/store timestamps, message ID, system flag, body CRC, queue offset, commit-log offset, store size, reconsume count, and prepared-transaction offset. Boundary inputs include signed integer/long minima and maxima. Updated the Phase 8 forward/reverse matrix, checksum and release checklist. Fixture SHA-256: `b54376335efed4d18ff547bec25c6c011aba89e34d78a576b432db666d293520`.
- Validation: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-common --all-features --locked` PASS (21 unit, 18 message differential, 1 topic-validator, 14 doctests); strict Common all-target/all-feature Clippy PASS; fmt/diff checks PASS; pinned offline Maven `verify` PASS (37 scenarios, fixture drift, Java/Rust cross-decodes).

- Message direct setter API audit slice (`2026-10-15`): added invoked Java/Rust differential coverage for `get/setTags`, `get/setKeys(String)`, `isWaitStoreMsgOK/setWaitStoreMsgOK`, and `get/setTransactionId`. Cases compare null entries, transaction-ID clearing, and the previous `WAIT` value returned by Rust's replacement operation; the Phase 8 matrix now records forward and reverse mappings. Fixture SHA-256: `dd291975d5c9da29101cbdf8f663fee2089fae9ec75802c78916701f039ad34a`.
- Validation: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-common --all-features --locked` PASS (21 unit, 18 message differential, 1 topic-validator, 14 doctests); strict Common all-target/all-feature Clippy PASS; fmt/diff PASS; Maven `verify` PASS (37 scenarios, fixture drift and Java/Rust cross-decodes). Initial Java compilation reported the intentional null `setKeys` call was ambiguous between String and Collection overloads; the fixture now casts null to String and test-compile/verification pass.
- `MessageClientExt` public API compatibility slice (`2026-10-15`): added an owned Rust view over `MessageExt` matching Java 5.5.1's no-op `setMsgId`, live `UNIQ_KEY` getter preference, physical-ID fallback, and mutable offset-ID methods. Added an invoked Java fixture and Rust differential, updated the Phase 8 method matrix, fixture checksum, and release checklist. Fixture SHA-256: `195a465e232a4eff25b4b713c4988f3103f1f9835e635371441a83e70b537eeb`.
- Validation: Common all-features tests PASS (21 unit, 19 message differential, 1 topic-validator, 14 doctests); strict Common all-target/all-feature Clippy PASS; `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` PASS; pinned offline Maven `verify` PASS (37 scenarios, fixture drift checks, and Java/Rust cross-decodes). The first focused Rust run used the pre-regeneration fixture and failed on the missing case; regenerated from the pinned Java fixture and reran successfully. Final review removed a duplicate Java import; no behavior changed.
- This closes the `MessageClientExt` API slice only. Full P18-V01 bidirectional source/API/input/error/flow and inherited/trait audit, final-revision full P18-V02, current GitHub Ubuntu address-profile evidence, native Windows stack runtime, Phase 19 Docker/Broker runner and scenarios, and release version/registry dependency resolution remain open. Final owner/production checks remain for the last manual-validation phase.
- `MessageQueue` method crosswalk audit (`2026-10-15`): confirmed the pinned Java constructors/copy constructor, field accessors, equality, hash, text and ordering paths are already exercised by invoked `messageQueueMethods`/`messageQueueCompareTo` fixtures and Rust differential tests. Added the missing Phase 8 matrix row and release-checklist disposition; no implementation or test change was needed. The broad P18-V01 audit remains open.
- Reverse-export follow-up (`2026-10-15`): removed unused public `MessageClientExt::as_message_ext` / `as_message_ext_mut` convenience methods; Java has no corresponding API and `Deref` already supplies inherited access. This narrows the just-added wrapper surface; broader P18-V01 reverse-export checks remain open.
- `MessageClientIDSetter` reverse-scan finding (`2026-10-15`): its Java 5.5.1 public surface includes `getNearlyTimeFromID`, `getIPStrFromID`, `getIPFromID`, and `getPidFromID`, beyond the generation/set/get paths previously mapped in the Phase 7 matrix. Rust has no full decode-helper mapping yet; its month-relative generator uses UTC month start while Java `Calendar` uses the process-local timezone. Recorded these as open P18-V01 work in the Phase 7 matrix and release checklist.
- `MessageClientIDSetter` helper parity slice (`2026-10-15`): added Rust IP/PID/time decoders, Java-compatible malformed-hex handling and fake-IP helper; unique-ID generation and time reconstruction now use the process-local calendar month boundary. Added invoked Java IPv4/IPv6 fixtures and Rust differentials; fixture SHA-256 `22a63de653583d5592d521d0a0bddddcb3506bf4253dd0d59b6bcf9269a81c39`. Validation: Core all-feature tests, strict Core all-target/all-feature Clippy, format, pinned offline Maven verify (37 scenarios and Java/Rust cross-decodes), and diff checks PASS. The public-helper differential passes in both the default GMT environment and `TZ=Asia/Taipei`. The first regeneration run exposed that the hand-built IDs were two bytes short; corrected their layout against Java's decoded IP/PID fields. The first Maven attempt then hit the stale `--locked` Cargo graph; offline resolution showed uncached `num_threads`, fetched it without changing its locked version, and the subsequent locked gates passed. This closes the identified helper slice only; broad P18-V01 remains open.
- Producer follow-up validation for the unique-ID timezone/layout change: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer --all-features --locked` PASS (142 unit tests, 10 admin, 27 Producer API, 3 request/reply, 17 scripted-send, 7 transaction tests, and 6 doctests); strict Producer all-target/all-feature Clippy PASS.
